cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "How accurate is altitude from pressure geolocators? A global validation of GeoPressureR altitude against station barometers and radiosondes"
abstract: >-
  Validation of the altitude that GeoPressureR and GeoPressureAPI retrieve from a pressure
  measurement using ERA5 reanalysis, against HadISD surface station barometers (ground level)
  and IGRA2 radiosondes (0-6 km above ground). Separates accuracy (static per-site bias) from
  precision (temporal scatter), quantifies their drivers, and compares ERA5 single-levels with
  ERA5-Land.
authors:
